BT /F2 11 Tf 0.12 0.22 0.4 rg 50 332.0 Td (1.1 What Is Programming Thinking vs. Coding?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 316.0 Td (Definition) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 302.0 Td (**Coding** is the act of writing instructions in a programming language. Any person can learn) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 290.5 Td (to write C# syntax within weeks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 275.0 Td (**Programming Thinking** is the cognitive discipline of modeling real-world problems as) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 263.5 Td (precise, executable logic - before writing a single line of code. It is the ability to see a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 252.0 Td (messy business requirement and transform it into clean, maintainable, correct logic.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 236.5 Td (A junior developer reads: *"Process an order payment and notify the user."*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 221.0 Td (They open Visual Studio and start typing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 205.5 Td (A senior developer reads the same requirement and first asks:) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 192.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 190.0 Td (What does "process" mean? Charge the card? Reserve funds? Both?) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 179.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 177.0 Td (What if the payment provider is down?) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 166.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 164.0 Td (What if the user's email is invalid?) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 153.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 151.0 Td (What is the rollback strategy?) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 140.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 138.0 Td (Who calls this? A web request? A queue consumer? A cron job?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 125.0 Td (That gap in thinking - not in syntax - is the difference between junior and senior.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 109.5 Td (Historical Reason) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 95.5 Td (Early computing \(1950s-1970s\) was dominated by mathematicians and engineers who wrote programs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 84.0 Td (as mathematical proofs. They had no choice but to think rigorously - memory was measured in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 72.5 Td (kilobytes, and bugs could crash physical hardware.) Tj ET
