BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 292.5 Td (#### Pillar 2: Abstraction Layers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 277.0 Td (**Definition:** Abstraction is the art of hiding complexity behind a simpler interface. Each) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 265.5 Td (layer of your system should only know what it needs to know.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 250.0 Td (**Why it exists:** A payment processing system in the 1990s was directly coupled to a single) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 238.5 Td (bank's mainframe API. When the bank changed their protocol, the entire application broke.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 227.0 Td (Engineers realized they needed a layer of abstraction - a "payment interface" - that could swap) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 215.5 Td (implementations.) Tj ET
