BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 326.5 Td (**Q:** "Does SRP mean a class should have only one method?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 311.0 Td (**A:** No. SRP is about *cohesion of concerns*, not method count. A `CustomerAccount` class can) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 299.5 Td (have `Deposit\(\)`, `Withdraw\(\)`, `GetBalance\(\)`, and `GetTransactionHistory\(\)` - all related to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 288.0 Td (one concern \(account state\). That does not violate SRP.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 272.5 Td (When to Violate SRP Intentionally) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 258.5 Td (In a startup with 3 developers and a 2-week deadline, over-engineering into 15 classes for a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 247.0 Td (simple feature is counterproductive. Pragmatic engineering sometimes accepts temporary SRP) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 235.5 Td (violations as *technical debt* - explicitly documented and scheduled for refactoring.) Tj ET
