BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 154.5 Td (      Software entities should be open for extension, but closed for modification.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 131.5 Td (You should be able to add new behavior without changing existing, tested code.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 116.0 Td (Historical Reason) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 102.0 Td (Bertrand Meyer introduced this in 1988. In large software products \(compilers, operating) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 90.5 Td (systems\), changing core modules for every new feature was catastrophic - it destabilized) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 79.0 Td (everything that depended on that module. The insight: design modules so new features *extend*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 67.5 Td (them, not *edit* them.) Tj ET
