0.85 0.88 0.92 RG 0.5 w 60 770.0 m 545 770.0 l S
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.12 0.22 0.4 rg 50 744.0 Td (5.1 What Is Software Architecture?) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 728.0 Td (Definition) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 714.0 Td (Software architecture is the set of **significant design decisions** that shape a system -) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 702.5 Td (decisions that are hard to change later. It defines:) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 689.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 687.0 Td (How components are organized and communicate) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 676.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 674.0 Td (How data flows through the system) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 663.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 661.0 Td (How the system grows, scales, and recovers from failure) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 650.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 648.0 Td (Which concerns are separated from which) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 635.0 Td (Architecture is not the same as design. Design is about *how* you implement. Architecture is) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 623.5 Td (about *what* you build and *where* responsibilities live.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 608.0 Td (The Architect's Core Questions) Tj ET
0.06 0.08 0.12 rg 50 528.5 495 65.5 re f
0.15 0.2 0.3 RG 0.5 w 50 528.5 495 65.5 re s
0.1 0.14 0.2 rg 50 580.0 495 14 re f
