BT /F2 11 Tf 0.12 0.22 0.4 rg 50 247.5 Td (Programming Thinking - Interview Questions) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 231.5 Td (**Basic:**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 216.0 Td (Q: What is the difference between programming and coding?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 200.5 Td (A: Coding is writing syntax. Programming is the thinking process of modeling a problem as) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 189.0 Td (executable logic - including problem decomposition, edge case analysis, and trade-off evaluation) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 177.5 Td (- before writing any code.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 162.0 Td (**Intermediate:**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 146.5 Td (Q: How do you approach a requirement you've never seen before?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 131.0 Td (A: I use the PRIMED framework: clarify the problem, establish requirements \(functional and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 119.5 Td (non-functional\), define inputs/outputs, draw a mental model, enumerate edge cases, then choose) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 108.0 Td (the simplest design that satisfies requirements. I resist the urge to code immediately.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 92.5 Td (**Senior Follow-up:**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 77.0 Td (Q: What's the most important question to ask when you receive a new feature request?) Tj ET
