BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 724.5 Td (**Inversion of Control \(IoC\)** is a fundamental architectural principle in which the control) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 713.0 Td (flow of a program is inverted: instead of a component instantiating its own dependencies) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 701.5 Td (directly, external infrastructure injects those dependencies at runtime.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 686.0 Td (**Dependency Injection \(DI\)** is the concrete design pattern used to realize IoC. In modern) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 674.5 Td (.NET, the DI engine is not an afterthought or a third-party plugin-it is baked into the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 663.0 Td (foundation via the `Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection` \(MEDI\) library. Every ASP.NET Core) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 651.5 Td (subsystem \(Kestrel, Logging, Routing, Entity Framework Core\) relies entirely on MEDI.) Tj ET
