BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 502.0 Td (#### Topic 1: Execution Pipeline & JIT Internals) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 488.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 486.5 Td (**Basic Question:** What is the difference between IL and Native Machine Code?) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 475.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 473.5 Td (**3 YOE Expected Answer:** C# code is compiled by the Roslyn compiler into Intermediate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 462.5 Td (Language \(IL\), which is platform-agnostic bytecode. When the application runs, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 451.5 Td (Just-In-Time \(JIT\) compiler compiles the IL into native machine instructions specific to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 440.5 Td (the host CPU architecture \(x86, x64, ARM\).) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 429.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 427.5 Td (**Senior Follow-up Question:** How does Tiered Compilation work in CoreCLR, and what role) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 416.5 Td (does Dynamic PGO play?) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 405.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 403.5 Td (**Senior Answer:** CoreCLR uses RyuJIT with a two-tiered compilation strategy:) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 392.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 390.5 Td (*Tier 0 \(Quick JIT\):* Compiles methods instantly without optimization to accelerate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 379.5 Td (startup. Methods are instrumented with invocation counters.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 368.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 366.5 Td (*Tier 1 \(Optimized JIT\):* Once a method crosses invocation thresholds \(typically 30) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 355.5 Td (calls\) or runs inside a hot loop \(OSR\), the background JIT recompiles it with full) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 344.5 Td (optimizations \(inlining, loop unrolling, SIMD\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 331.5 Td (*Dynamic PGO \(Profile Guided Optimization\)* takes this further: Tier 0 collects runtime data) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 320.0 Td (\(concrete types executing through interfaces, branch probabilities\). Tier 1 then performs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 308.5 Td (**Guarded Devirtualization \(GDV\)**, replacing slow polymorphic virtual calls with direct,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 297.0 Td (inlined method calls guarded by a single pointer comparison.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 283.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 281.5 Td (**Interviewer Trap:** "If JIT compiles IL to machine code at runtime, why does a method) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 270.5 Td (execute slower the very first time it is invoked, and how do you eliminate this in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 259.5 Td (high-frequency trading systems?") Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 248.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 246.5 Td (**Master Trap Answer:** The first invocation incurs a **JIT compilation pause** because) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 235.5 Td (the method's VTable entry points to a JIT Pre-Stub. When hit, the Pre-Stub compiles the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 224.5 Td (IL, updates the method pointer in the MethodTable, and then executes the code.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 211.5 Td (To eliminate this in latency-sensitive systems:) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 198.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 196.0 Td (Use **ReadyToRun \(R2R\)** to pre-compile IL into native code at build time.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 185.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 183.0 Td (Execute warmup routines at application boot using) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 172.0 Td (`RuntimeHelpers.PrepareMethod\(method.MethodHandle\)` to force Tier 1 JIT compilation before) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 161.0 Td (traffic is routed to the node.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 150.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 148.0 Td (Use **Native AOT** to pre-compile the entire application ahead-of-time.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 135.0 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 119.5 Td (#### Topic 2: Dependency Injection & Lifetimes) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 106.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 104.0 Td (**Basic Question:** What are the three service lifetimes in ASP.NET Core?) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 93.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 91.0 Td (**3 YOE Expected Answer:** Transient \(new instance every time requested\), Scoped \(one) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 80.0 Td (instance per HTTP request scope\), and Singleton \(one instance shared across the entire) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 69.0 Td (application\).) Tj ET
