0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 792.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 790.0 Td (**Senior Follow-up Question:** What is a Captive Dependency, and what are its exact) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 779.0 Td (real-world consequences on an Entity Framework `DbContext`?) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 768.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 766.0 Td (**Senior Answer:** A Captive Dependency occurs when a service with a longer lifetime) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 755.0 Td (captures a service with a shorter lifetime \(e.g., a Singleton capturing a Scoped service\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 742.0 Td (If a Singleton captures an EF Core `DbContext`:) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 728.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 726.5 Td (*Concurrency Exceptions:* `DbContext` is not thread-safe. Multiple simultaneous HTTP) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 715.5 Td (requests will invoke methods on the same captured instance, triggering) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 704.5 Td (`InvalidOperationException: A second operation was started on this context before a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 693.5 Td (previous operation completed`.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 682.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 680.5 Td (*Memory Leak:* The `DbContext` Change Tracker will retain entity instances indefinitely) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 669.5 Td (in Gen 2 heap memory.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 658.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 656.5 Td (*Data Corruption:* Stale entities cached in the first-level cache will be returned across) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 645.5 Td (different users' requests.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 634.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 632.5 Td (**Interviewer Trap:** "Can a Transient service cause a memory leak if it implements) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 621.5 Td (`IDisposable`? Why?") Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 610.5 3 3 re f
