BT /F2 8 Tf 0.1 0.65 0.35 rg 62 449.5 Td ([TIP]) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 449.5 Td (      *Best Answer:* Strings are immutable for security, thread safety, and hash consistency.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 438.5 Td (Thread safety is guaranteed because multiple threads can read a string without locking.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 427.5 Td (Security is ensured because sensitive values like connection strings, file paths, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 416.5 Td (security tokens cannot be tampered with after validation. Immutability also allows) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 405.5 Td (strings to serve as stable keys in hash tables without their hash codes mutating.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 384.5 3 3 re f
