BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 650.0 Td (Invoking `GC.SuppressFinalize\(this\)` toggles a bit in the object's runtime header, instructing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 638.5 Td (the GC to delete its entry from the Finalization Queue. When the object dies, it bypasses the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 627.0 Td (`Freachable` queue entirely and is reclaimed in a single GC pass without promotion.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 611.5 Td (#### `SafeHandle` vs. Custom Finalizers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 596.0 Td (Writing a custom finalizer \(`~ClassName\(\)`\) is considered an anti-pattern in modern .NET. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 584.5 Td (CLR provides `SafeHandle` \(`System.Runtime.InteropServices`\), which inherits from) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 573.0 Td (`CriticalFinalizerObject`. `SafeHandle` guarantees:) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 559.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 557.5 Td (**Critical Finalization**: The runtime compiles the finalizer code in advance; it will) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 546.5 Td (execute even in out-of-memory or thread-abort conditions.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 535.5 3 3 re f
