BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 469.5 Td (8. Design Reasoning) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 455.5 Td (The separation into `Dispose\(bool disposing\)` addresses a crucial invariant: **Never touch) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 444.0 Td (managed objects inside a Finalizer**. When `disposing == false`, the code is executing on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 432.5 Td (CLR Finalizer thread. The GC makes *no guarantees* about the order in which objects are) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 421.0 Td (finalized. Any managed field referenced on that object might have already been finalized and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 409.5 Td (destroyed; accessing it can cause `NullReferenceException` or crash the runtime.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 394.0 Td (9. Performance Impact) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 382.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 380.0 Td (An object with an active Finalizer that is not suppressed costs **at least $2\\times$ more) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 369.0 Td (GC overhead**, as it is forced to survive into Gen 1 or Gen 2.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 358.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 356.0 Td (Suppressed objects cost 0 additional bytes and zero promotion penalties.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 345.0 3 3 re f
