BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 747.5 Td (*Answer*: An array is a heap-allocated reference type subject to GC tracking and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 736.5 Td (overhead. `Span<T>` is a stack-only `ref struct` that provides a type-safe, contiguous) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 725.5 Td (view of any memory \(managed, stack, or native\) without allocating memory. Slicing an array) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 714.5 Td (copies elements or creates a new array; slicing a `Span<T>` is a zero-allocation operation) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 703.5 Td (that simply adjusts an interior pointer and length.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 692.5 3 3 re f
