0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 679.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 677.5 Td (*Answer*: `Span<T>` is a `ref struct` that can contain interior pointers to the execution) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 666.5 Td (stack. If a class \(which lives on the heap\) were allowed to hold a `Span<T>`, the stack) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 655.5 Td (frame where the memory was allocated could unwind while the heap class continued to hold) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 644.5 Td (the pointer, leading to a dangling pointer and memory corruption. The CLR enforces that) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 633.5 Td (`ref struct` instances can only reside on the stack.) Tj ET
