BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 321.0 Td (2. Historical Reason) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 307.0 Td (By default in C#, value types \(`struct`\) are passed by value: the entire binary representation) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 295.5 Td (of the struct is copied onto the called method's stack frame. For small primitives \(`int`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 284.0 Td (`bool`, `Guid`\), this is trivial. However, for large mathematical, audio, or financial data) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 272.5 Td (structs \(e.g., a 64-byte or 128-byte Matrix or OrderBook struct\), copying the struct on every) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 261.0 Td (method call consumes significant CPU instructions and memory bandwidth. C# introduced `in`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 249.5 Td (parameters and `ref returns` to eliminate struct copying without sacrificing immutability.) Tj ET
