BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 649.5 Td (When you pass a struct with the `in` modifier, the compiler guarantees that the callee cannot) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 638.0 Td (mutate the struct.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 622.5 Td (However, if the struct is declared as a standard struct \(not a `readonly struct`\), **the C#) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 611.0 Td (compiler cannot trust that calling a method or property getter on that struct will not mutate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 599.5 Td (its internal state!**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 584.0 Td (To prevent mutation, the compiler creates a **Defensive Copy**: it silently copies the struct) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 572.5 Td (onto the local stack frame before executing any property or method!) Tj ET
