BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 386.5 Td (`async`/`await` is a compiler-transformed language abstraction that enables asynchronous,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 375.0 Td (non-blocking execution using synchronous-like control flow. Instead of spawning operating system) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 363.5 Td (threads, the Roslyn compiler rewrites async methods into state machines implementing the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 352.0 Td (`IAsyncStateMachine` interface. This releases OS threads back to the CLR `ThreadPool` during) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 340.5 Td (non-blocking asynchronous I/O waits and schedules continuations upon completion.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 325.0 Td (2. Historical Reason) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 311.0 Td (Prior to C# 5.0, asynchronous programming relied on two complex patterns:) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 297.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 295.5 Td (**Asynchronous Programming Model \(APM\)**: `BeginInvoke` / `EndInvoke` with) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 284.5 Td (`IAsyncResult`. Required manual state passing, was prone to memory leaks, and made error) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 273.5 Td (handling across multiple asynchronous calls nearly impossible.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 262.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 260.5 Td (**Event-Based Asynchronous Pattern \(EAP\)**: `MethodAsync\(\)` with a `MethodCompleted`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 249.5 Td (event handler. Created "callback hell", disrupted logical call stacks, and caused severe) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 238.5 Td (memory leaks due to unhooked event listeners.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 225.5 Td (Both models obscured business logic with boilerplate callback orchestration and lacked unified) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 214.0 Td (exception handling \(`try`/`catch`/`finally`\). `async`/`await` was introduced in C# 5.0 to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 202.5 Td (provide linear control flow, compile-time exception propagation, and thread-agnostic state) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 191.0 Td (management.) Tj ET
