BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 303.5 Td (**OS Thread**: An operating system execution context managed by the Windows/Linux kernel) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 292.5 Td (scheduler. Expensive to create, switch, and destroy.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 281.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 279.5 Td (**Task**: A lightweight user-space managed object representing a future promise of) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 268.5 Td (completion. Allocates less than 100 bytes and does not hold an OS thread while waiting.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 255.5 Td (#### ThreadPool Architecture: Global Queue vs. Local Work-Stealing Queues) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 240.0 Td (The CLR ThreadPool implements a two-tier work-scheduling architecture:) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 226.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 224.5 Td (**The Global Queue**: A single shared FIFO \(First-In, First-Out\) queue protected by a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 213.5 Td (global lock. Work queued from external non-pool threads \(or via) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 202.5 Td (`ThreadPool.QueueUserWorkItem`\) enters this queue.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 191.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 189.5 Td (**Per-Thread Local Work Queues**: Each ThreadPool worker thread possesses its own) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 178.5 Td (dedicated, lock-free work queue.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 167.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 165.5 Td (When a thread scheduled on a worker queues another Task \(e.g., `Task.Run` or an async) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 154.5 Td (continuation\), it pushes the work onto its own **Local Queue**.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 143.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 141.5 Td (**LIFO \(Last-In, First-Out\) Execution**: The owning thread pushes and pops tasks in LIFO) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 130.5 Td (order. LIFO maximizes **CPU cache locality**: data accessed by the most recent task is) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 119.5 Td (still warm in the processor's L1/L2 cache!) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 108.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 106.5 Td (**FIFO Work-Stealing**: When a worker thread's local queue is empty, it attempts to steal) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 95.5 Td (tasks from the *tails* of other worker threads' local queues using lock-free atomic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 84.5 Td (operations \(`Interlocked.CompareExchange`\) in **FIFO order**. If all local queues are) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 73.5 Td (empty, it dequeues work from the Global Queue.) Tj ET
