BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 587.0 Td (How does the ThreadPool decide whether to create more worker threads or terminate idle ones?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 571.5 Td (The CLR uses a mathematical control algorithm called **Hill Climbing**:) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 558.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 556.0 Td (It continuously monitors **System Throughput** \(number of completed work items per) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 545.0 Td (millisecond\).) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 534.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 532.0 Td (It introduces small perturbations in thread count \(e.g., adding 1-2 threads\).) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 521.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 519.0 Td (It measures the resulting throughput delta:) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 508.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 506.0 Td (If adding threads **increases throughput**, it injects more threads.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 495.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 493.0 Td (If adding threads **causes throughput to plateau or drop** \(due to lock contention or) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 482.0 Td (context switching\), it stops injecting and begins retiring threads.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 471.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 469.0 Td (**The Thread Injection Rate Limit**: When the pool is saturated, Hill Climbing injects) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 458.0 Td (threads very conservatively-approximately **one thread every 500 milliseconds \(1-2 threads) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 447.0 Td (per second\)**. If an application blocks 50 threads synchronously, it can take up to 25-50) Tj ET
