BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 192.0 Td (8. Design Reasoning) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 178.0 Td (The choice of **LIFO for the owning thread** and **FIFO for stealing threads** is an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 166.5 Td (algorithmic masterpiece:) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 153.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 151.0 Td (**LIFO for Owner**: The most recently created task has its working data stored in the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 140.0 Td (local CPU L1/L2 cache. Executing it immediately guarantees high cache-hit ratios and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 129.0 Td (minimal RAM latency.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 118.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 116.0 Td (**FIFO for Stealers**: Older tasks at the bottom of the queue are "coldest" in CPU cache.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 105.0 Td (If another core must steal work, it steals the oldest task, minimizing cache invalidation) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 94.0 Td (conflicts with the owner thread.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 81.0 Td (9. Performance Impact) Tj ET
