BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 353.0 Td (*Answer*: Creating OS threads is expensive in CPU cycles and memory \(1 MB stack per) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 342.0 Td (thread\). The CLR ThreadPool maintains a reusable pool of pre-allocated worker threads,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 331.0 Td (multiplexing many tasks over a small number of physical threads matching CPU capacity,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 320.0 Td (avoiding thread creation overhead and context switching thrashing.) Tj ET
