0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 296.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 294.0 Td (*Answer*: Each worker thread maintains its own lock-free local queue. The owning thread) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 283.0 Td (processes tasks in LIFO order to maximize CPU cache locality. When a worker runs out of) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 272.0 Td (work, it steals tasks from the tails of other threads' queues in FIFO order using atomic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 261.0 Td (compare-and-swap operations, ensuring load balancing across cores without global lock) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 250.0 Td (contention.) Tj ET
