0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 215.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 213.0 Td (*Answer*: Hill Climbing is the heuristic used by the ThreadPool to determine the optimal) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 202.0 Td (thread count by measuring throughput against thread variations. When threads block) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 191.0 Td (synchronously, the pool is starved of available workers. Hill Climbing injects replacement) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 180.0 Td (threads at a throttled rate \(~1-2 threads per second\) to prevent runaway context) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 169.0 Td (switching. If hundreds of items are queued, this injection delay causes multi-second queue) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 158.0 Td (latency, starving downstream continuations and health checks.) Tj ET
