BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 653.0 Td (pipelines. When multiple CPU cores execute simultaneously, writes made by Core 1 to its local L1) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 641.5 Td (cache or store buffer are not immediately visible to Core 2. Without synchronization and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 630.0 Td (hardware **memory barriers \(fences\)**, threads will read stale data, write corrupted bits, or) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 618.5 Td (execute instructions out of logical order. Synchronization primitives enforce memory barriers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 607.0 Td (and mutual exclusion.) Tj ET
