BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 170.0 Td (If an operation takes **less than 20 CPU cycles** \(e.g., updating a counter or swapping a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 159.0 Td (pointer\), using a lock or semaphore is an architectural failure. Use `Interlocked`.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 148.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 146.0 Td (If an operation takes **sub-microsecond duration** with near-zero contention, `Monitor`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 135.0 Td (\(`lock`\) is ideal due to thin-lock user-mode optimizations.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 124.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 122.0 Td (If an operation involves **asynchronous I/O \(`await`\)**, `SemaphoreSlim` is the *only*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 111.0 Td (valid choice because managed locks forbid asynchronous boundaries.) Tj ET
