BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 464.0 Td (11. Production Problems: Thread Starvation via Contended SpinLock) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 450.0 Td (**Incident**: A high-frequency payment switch server experienced 100% CPU utilization across) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 438.5 Td (all 32 cores, while transaction throughput collapsed to zero.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 423.0 Td (**Root Cause**: A developer attempted to optimize an in-memory ledger by replacing a standard) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 411.5 Td (`lock` with a `SpinLock`. Under light benchmark loads, `SpinLock` appeared faster. However, in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 400.0 Td (production, a thread holding the `SpinLock` was preempted by the OS thread scheduler because its) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 388.5 Td (execution quantum expired. While that thread was suspended, 31 other worker threads attempted to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 377.0 Td (acquire the `SpinLock`. Because a `SpinLock` actively spins in a tight CPU loop rather than) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 365.5 Td (yielding the processor, all 31 CPU cores pinned at 100% utilization doing zero productive work.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 350.0 Td (**Post-Mortem Resolution**: Banned `SpinLock` across business code. Migrated to `Monitor`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 338.5 Td (\(`lock`\) and `Interlocked.CompareExchange` loops.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 323.0 Td (12. Interview Prep) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 311.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 309.0 Td (**Basic**: "What is the difference between `lock` and `Monitor`?") Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 298.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 296.0 Td (*Answer*: `lock \(obj\)` is syntactic sugar provided by the C# compiler that expands to a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 285.0 Td (`Monitor.Enter\(obj, ref lockTaken\)` wrapped in a `try/finally` block that calls) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 274.0 Td (`Monitor.Exit\(obj\)` in the `finally` block. `Monitor` also exposes advanced coordination) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 263.0 Td (capabilities such as `Wait\(\)`, `Pulse\(\)`, and `PulseAll\(\)`.) Tj ET
