BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 240.0 Td (*Answer*: A deadlock is a state where two or more threads are permanently blocked because) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 229.0 Td (each holds a lock that the other needs. It is caused by meeting the four Coffman) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 218.0 Td (conditions: mutual exclusion, hold and wait, no preemption, and circular wait.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 207.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 205.0 Td (**Intermediate**: "What is the Sync-Over-Async anti-pattern and why is it dangerous?") Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 194.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 192.0 Td (*Answer*: Sync-Over-Async occurs when synchronous blocking calls \(`.Result`, `.Wait\(\)`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 181.0 Td (`.GetAwaiter\(\).GetResult\(\)`\) are invoked on asynchronous methods. In environments with a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 170.0 Td (`SynchronizationContext` \(like WPF or legacy ASP.NET\), it causes an immediate circular) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 159.0 Td (deadlock. In ASP.NET Core, it causes ThreadPool starvation by blocking worker threads) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 148.0 Td (waiting on continuations that require worker threads to execute.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 137.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 135.0 Td (**Senior**: "How do you systematically prevent deadlocks in complex multi-resource) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 124.0 Td (locking architectures?") Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 113.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 111.0 Td (*Answer*: By breaking the **Circular Wait** condition through **Global Lock Ordering**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 100.0 Td (all locks are assigned a deterministic sequence \(such as ascending resource ID order\),) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 89.0 Td (ensuring every thread acquires locks in the exact same sequence. Additionally, using) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 78.0 Td (`Monitor.TryEnter` with timeouts prevents permanent blocking, and replacing synchronous) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 67.0 Td (multi-threaded locks with single-writer architectures \(Channels or Actor models\)) Tj ET
