0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 382.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 380.0 Td (*Answer*: `Queue<T>` is a synchronous, non-thread-safe collection.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 369.0 Td (`System.Threading.Channels` is a high-performance, asynchronous, thread-safe communication) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 358.0 Td (primitive for producer-consumer pipelines that supports non-blocking async reads/writes,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 347.0 Td (backpressure, and zero-allocation streaming via `ValueTask`.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 336.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 334.0 Td (**Intermediate**: "What is Backpressure in the context of bounded channels?") Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 323.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 321.0 Td (*Answer*: Backpressure is a flow-control mechanism that occurs when consumers cannot keep) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 310.0 Td (pace with producers. In a bounded channel with `BoundedChannelFullMode.Wait`, when the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 299.0 Td (queue reaches capacity, further calls to `WriteAsync` asynchronously suspend the producer) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 288.0 Td (until consumers read items and create space, preventing runaway memory consumption.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 277.0 3 3 re f
