BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 740.0 Td (**Parallel Programming** in .NET executes computationally intensive \(CPU-bound\) workloads) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 728.5 Td (concurrently across multiple CPU cores to minimize total execution time. It encompasses the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 717.0 Td (**Task Parallel Library \(TPL\)** \(`Parallel.For`, `Parallel.ForEach`, `Parallel.ForEachAsync`\),) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 705.5 Td (**Parallel LINQ \(PLINQ\)**, and **TPL Dataflow** actor-based pipeline blocks.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 690.0 Td (2. Historical Reason) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 676.0 Td (Prior to .NET 4.0, executing parallel computation across multiple cores required manual thread) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 664.5 Td (division, index calculation, and error aggregation. With multi-core processors becoming) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 653.0 Td (standard, developers needed a framework that automatically partitioned datasets, balanced) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 641.5 Td (workloads across CPU cores, and abstracted away thread lifecycles.) Tj ET
