BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 397.5 Td (patients following a scheduled batch run, but reported "Batch Succeeded" in its audit log.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 382.0 Td (**Root Cause**: A developer refactored the dispatch loop to use `Parallel.ForEach`:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 366.5 Td (`Parallel.ForEach\(alerts, async alert => await _smsService.SendAsync\(alert\)\);`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 351.0 Td (Because `Parallel.ForEach` accepts an `Action<T>`, passing an `async` lambda caused the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 339.5 Td (compiler to treat it as `async void`. `Parallel.ForEach` launched the iterations and immediately) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 328.0 Td (returned without awaiting completion! The background thread finished, and the service terminated) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 316.5 Td (the process, killing all active network socket connections before the SMS messages were) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 305.0 Td (transmitted.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 289.5 Td (**Post-Mortem Resolution**: Migrated all asynchronous iteration loops to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 278.0 Td (`Parallel.ForEachAsync` and enforced compiler warnings preventing `async void` lambda) Tj ET
