BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 237.0 Td (**Basic**: "What is the difference between concurrency and parallelism?") Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 226.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 224.0 Td (*Answer*: Concurrency is about *dealing with* lots of things at once \(e.g., interleaving) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 213.0 Td (tasks, handling asynchronous I/O without blocking threads\). Parallelism is about *doing*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 202.0 Td (lots of things at once \(e.g., simultaneously utilizing multiple physical CPU cores to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 191.0 Td (execute heavy computations\).) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 180.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 178.0 Td (**Intermediate**: "Why should you never pass an `async` lambda to `Parallel.ForEach`, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 167.0 Td (what should you use instead?") Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 156.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 154.0 Td (*Answer*: `Parallel.ForEach` only accepts synchronous `Action<T>` delegates. Passing an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 143.0 Td (`async` lambda causes it to be compiled as `async void`. `Parallel.ForEach` will not await) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 132.0 Td (the tasks, returning immediately while work is still in flight, and any exceptions thrown) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 121.0 Td (will crash the process or go unobserved. In .NET 6+, always use `Parallel.ForEachAsync`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 110.0 Td (which is natively designed to await asynchronous delegates.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 99.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 97.0 Td (**Senior**: "How does exception handling work in `Task.WhenAll`, and how do you prevent) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 86.0 Td (swallowing inner exceptions?") Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 75.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 73.0 Td (*Answer*: When multiple tasks passed to `Task.WhenAll` fault, all exceptions are captured) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 62.0 Td (into an `AggregateException`. However, when you `await Task.WhenAll\(tasks\)`, the C#) Tj ET
