BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 289.0 Td (1. Definition) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 275.0 Td (Encapsulation is **bundling data \(state\) and behavior \(methods\) together** inside a class,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 263.5 Td (while **controlling external access** to that data. It is NOT simply "making fields private" -) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 252.0 Td (that is *information hiding*, a related but distinct concept.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 236.5 Td (**Encapsulation = Data + Behavior bound together**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 221.0 Td (**Information Hiding = Deciding what to expose and what to protect**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 205.5 Td (Both work together. You encapsulate by putting balance and Deposit\(\) in the same class. You) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 194.0 Td (hide by making balance private.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 178.5 Td (2. Historical Reason) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 164.5 Td (Before OOP, programs were written procedurally: data structures \(`struct`\) held data and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 153.0 Td (separate functions operated on them. Any function could modify any data. This led to:) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 139.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 137.5 Td (Impossible-to-trace bugs \(who changed this value?\)) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 126.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 124.5 Td (No invariants enforced \(balance went negative\)) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 113.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 111.5 Td (Global state disasters) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 98.5 Td (OOP was invented specifically to give data *owners* - to say "this data belongs to this object,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 87.0 Td (and only this object manages it.") Tj ET
