BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 707.0 Td (12. Interview Prep) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 693.0 Td (**Basic:** "What is encapsulation?") Tj ET
0.94 0.96 0.99 rg 50 630.5 495 47 re f
0.15 0.45 0.85 rg 50 630.5 4 47 re f
0.85 0.88 0.92 RG 0.5 w 50 630.5 495 47 re s
BT /F2 8 Tf 0.15 0.45 0.85 rg 62 667.5 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 667.5 Td (      Encapsulation bundles data and behavior together in a class and controls external) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 656.5 Td (access through access modifiers and properties. It's not just making fields private -) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 645.5 Td (it's about the class *owning* its state and enforcing business invariants.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 622.5 Td (**Intermediate:** "What's the difference between encapsulation and information hiding?") Tj ET
0.94 0.96 0.99 rg 50 549.0 495 58 re f
0.15 0.45 0.85 rg 50 549.0 4 58 re f
0.85 0.88 0.92 RG 0.5 w 50 549.0 495 58 re s
BT /F2 8 Tf 0.15 0.45 0.85 rg 62 597.0 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 597.0 Td (      Encapsulation is about grouping data and behavior together. Information hiding is about) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 586.0 Td (what you expose. They work together: you encapsulate a `BankAccount` \(data + methods in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 575.0 Td (one class\), and you hide the `_balance` field \(information hiding\) so external code) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 564.0 Td (can't corrupt it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 541.0 Td (**Senior:** "How does encapsulation relate to the design of domain models?") Tj ET
0.94 0.96 0.99 rg 50 456.5 495 69 re f
0.15 0.45 0.85 rg 50 456.5 4 69 re f
0.85 0.88 0.92 RG 0.5 w 50 456.5 495 69 re s
BT /F2 8 Tf 0.15 0.45 0.85 rg 62 515.5 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 515.5 Td (      A well-encapsulated domain model is a Rich Domain Model where invariants are enforced) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 504.5 Td (by the object itself. The alternative is an Anemic Domain Model - objects are just data) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 493.5 Td (bags, and all logic lives in services. Anemic models violate encapsulation because the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 482.5 Td (data and its behavior are separated. In DDD, entities and aggregates should encapsulate) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 471.5 Td (their state transitions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 448.5 Td (**Tricky:** "Can you have encapsulation without OOP?") Tj ET
0.94 0.96 0.99 rg 50 386.0 495 47 re f
0.15 0.45 0.85 rg 50 386.0 4 47 re f
0.85 0.88 0.92 RG 0.5 w 50 386.0 495 47 re s
BT /F2 8 Tf 0.15 0.45 0.85 rg 62 423.0 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 423.0 Td (      Yes. Closures in functional languages encapsulate state. Modules in non-OOP languages) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 412.0 Td (can encapsulate. OOP formalizes it with classes, but the concept is architectural, not) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 401.0 Td (language-specific.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 378.0 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.12 0.22 0.4 rg 50 352.5 Td (Inheritance) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 336.5 Td (1. Definition) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 322.5 Td (Inheritance is a mechanism where a **derived class \(child\)** acquires the properties and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 311.0 Td (behaviors of a **base class \(parent\)**. It creates an **IS-A relationship**.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 295.5 Td (2. Historical Reason) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 281.5 Td (In the 1980s-90s, inheritance was seen as the primary code reuse mechanism. "Don't rewrite) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 270.0 Td (PaymentProcessor logic - inherit from it." This led to massive, deep hierarchies. By the 2000s,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 258.5 Td (the industry recognized the problems and began favoring composition. Inheritance still has a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 247.0 Td (place but requires careful judgment.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 231.5 Td (3. Problem It Solves \(and Creates\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 217.5 Td (**Legitimate use:** Polymorphism - treating different subtypes uniformly through a base type) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 206.0 Td (reference.) Tj ET
