BT /F2 8 Tf 0.15 0.45 0.85 rg 62 297.0 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 297.0 Td (      There's no fixed number. The guidance is: as many methods as a single CLIENT ROLE) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 286.0 Td (needs, no more. A `IOrderReader` might have 5 methods if all 5 are needed by every read) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 275.0 Td (client. The rule isn't "one method per interface" \(that leads to interface explosion\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 264.0 Td (It's "don't force clients to depend on methods they don't use." In practice, I design) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 253.0 Td (interfaces from the consumer's perspective: what does this client actually need?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 230.0 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 0.12 0.22 0.4 rg 50 204.5 Td (D - Dependency Inversion Principle) Tj ET
