BT /F2 11 Tf 0.12 0.22 0.4 rg 50 159.0 Td (What DI Really Is) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 143.0 Td (Dependency Injection is the technique of providing an object's dependencies from *outside*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 131.5 Td (rather than letting the object create them. It implements the Dependency Inversion Principle and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 120.0 Td (the Inversion of Control principle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 104.5 Td (**IoC \(Inversion of Control\):** Control of object creation is inverted - the framework controls) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 93.0 Td (it, not your code.) Tj ET
