BT /F2 8 Tf 0.15 0.45 0.85 rg 62 157.0 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 157.0 Td (      DI is a technique where a class receives its dependencies from outside rather than) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 146.0 Td (creating them itself. This makes classes testable, configurable, and loosely coupled. In) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 135.0 Td (.NET, the built-in DI container manages object creation and lifetime.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 112.0 Td (**Intermediate:** "What is the Captive Dependency Problem?") Tj ET
