BT /F2 8 Tf 0.15 0.45 0.85 rg 62 595.0 Td ([NOTE]) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 595.0 Td (      DI is one implementation of IoC. IoC is the broader principle: control of something) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 584.0 Td (\(object creation, program flow\) is inverted from your code to the framework. DI) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 573.0 Td (specifically inverts control of dependency creation. Other IoC examples: event systems) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 562.0 Td (\(framework calls your handlers\), template method \(framework calls your override\),) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.2 Tf 0.15 0.2 0.25 rg 62 551.0 Td (iterator pattern.) Tj ET
