BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 714.5 Td (1. Definition) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 700.5 Td (The **ASP.NET Core Request Lifecycle** is the end-to-end processing pipeline through which an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 689.0 Td (incoming raw TCP byte stream arrives at the operating system network stack, is accepted by the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 677.5 Td (cross-platform **Kestrel** web server, is parsed into managed abstractions \(`HttpContext`,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 666.0 Td (`HttpRequest`, `HttpResponse`\), traverses a bi-directional middleware pipeline, executes an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 654.5 Td (application endpoint \(Minimal API or Controller action with filters\), and serializes a binary) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 643.0 Td (response back over the physical socket.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 627.5 Td (2. Historical Reason) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 613.5 Td (In legacy .NET Framework \(ASP.NET MVC 5 / Web API 2\):) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 600.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 598.0 Td (Web applications were hard-coupled to Windows Internet Information Services \(**IIS**\) and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 587.0 Td (the native worker process \(`w3wp.exe`\).) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 576.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 574.0 Td (Hosting relied on `System.Web.dll`, a monolithic 20-year-old assembly tightly coupled to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 563.0 Td (COM and Windows OS APIs.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 552.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 550.0 Td (The legacy `HttpContext` was a massive, non-mockable object allocating megabytes of) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 539.0 Td (memory per request.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 528.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 526.0 Td (The pipeline was governed by `HttpRuntime` and 20+ hardcoded event stages) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 515.0 Td (\(`BeginRequest`, `AuthenticateRequest`, `AuthorizeRequest`, etc.\) that ran synchronously) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 504.0 Td (on OS threads, causing massive thread-pool starvation under high concurrent I/O.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 493.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 491.0 Td (**ASP.NET Core** abandoned `System.Web` completely. The architecture was rewritten from) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 480.0 Td (scratch around a lightweight, modular, cross-platform HTTP server called **Kestrel**,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 469.0 Td (enabling .NET to run natively on Linux, macOS, Docker containers, and Kubernetes clusters.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 456.0 Td (3. Problem It Solves) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 444.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 442.0 Td (**OS Independence**: Runs natively on Linux container runtimes without requiring Windows) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 431.0 Td (Server or IIS.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 420.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 418.0 Td (**Extreme Throughput & Low Latency**: Replaces synchronous blocking I/O with) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 407.0 Td (asynchronous, non-blocking socket handling built on `System.IO.Pipelines`, eliminating) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 396.0 Td (unnecessary buffer allocations and garbage collection pressure.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 385.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 383.0 Td (**Microservice Scalability**: Allows high-density packing of microservices inside) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 372.0 Td (container clusters \(Docker/Kubernetes\) due to tiny memory footprint \(~30MB base RSS) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 361.0 Td (compared to ~300MB in IIS\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 348.0 Td (4. Internal Working) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 336.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 334.0 Td (**Socket Binding & Transport Layer**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 321.0 Td (Kestrel uses the managed **Sockets Transport** \(default since .NET Core 2.1, replacing Libuv\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 309.5 Td (When Kestrel boots, it creates a `SocketConnectionListener` that binds to an IP address and port) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 298.0 Td (\(e.g., `0.0.0.0:5000`\).) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 284.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 282.5 Td (**Accepting Connections & Thread Pooling**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 269.5 Td (When a client completes the TCP three-way handshake \(`SYN`, `SYN-ACK`, `ACK`\), the OS socket) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 258.0 Td (triggers an asynchronous accept operation. A dedicated transport worker pulls the connection off) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 246.5 Td (the socket and schedules work onto the .NET `ThreadPool` without context-switching to native) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 235.0 Td (threads.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 221.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 219.5 Td (**Memory Management via System.IO.Pipelines**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 206.5 Td (Instead of allocating a new `byte[]` buffer per request or using standard `Stream`, Kestrel) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 195.0 Td (utilizes `System.IO.Pipelines`. It leases pooled memory slabs from `ArrayPool<byte>.Shared` and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 183.5 Td (`MemoryPool<byte>`.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 170.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 168.0 Td (**Zero-Allocation HTTP Parsing**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 155.0 Td (Kestrel's HTTP parser reads raw bytes directly from the `PipeReader` using) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 143.5 Td (`ReadOnlySequence<byte>`. It parses HTTP/1.1 verb, path, query strings, headers, or HTTP/2) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 132.0 Td (binary frames \(`HEADERS`, `DATA`, `SETTINGS`\) without allocating string instances where) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 120.5 Td (possible, utilizing interned strings and `Span<byte>`.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 107.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 105.0 Td (**Feature Collection & DefaultHttpContext**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 92.0 Td (Kestrel instantiates a `DefaultHttpContext` backed by an `IFeatureCollection`. The feature) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 80.5 Td (collection decouples the web server from the application. Low-level connection details) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 69.0 Td (\(`IHttpRequestFeature`, `IHttpResponseFeature`, `ITlsConnectionFeature`\) are wrapped as) Tj ET
