BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 790.0 Td (properties on `HttpContext`.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 776.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 774.5 Td (**Execution of the RequestDelegate**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 761.5 Td (Kestrel invokes the compiled pipeline root delegate: `RequestDelegate\(HttpContext\)`. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 750.0 Td (request flows sequentially down the middleware chain to the matched endpoint.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 736.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 734.5 Td (**Writing the Response**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 721.5 Td (When the endpoint finishes, the response body streams into the `PipeWriter` of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 710.0 Td (`HttpResponseStream`. The transport flushes the pooled memory blocks back to the TCP socket, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 698.5 Td (the leased memory blocks are returned to the `ArrayPool`.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 685.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 683.0 Td (**Connection Re-Use \(Keep-Alive\)**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 670.0 Td (If HTTP Keep-Alive is active \(or HTTP/2 multiplexing\), the socket remains open and waits for) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 658.5 Td (subsequent requests; otherwise, the connection is closed gracefully via TCP `FIN`.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 643.0 Td (5. Real Production Example: Payment Gateway Ingestion) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 629.0 Td (A payment ingestion gateway receives 45,000 webhook events per second from Stripe, PayPal, and) Tj ET
