BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 422.0 Td (8. Design Reasoning) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 410.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 408.0 Td (**The "Captive Dependency" Architecture**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 395.0 Td (In convention-based middleware, the class constructor is called **exactly once** during) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 383.5 Td (application startup when `IApplicationBuilder.Build\(\)` is executed. It is effectively a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 372.0 Td (**Singleton**. If you inject a `Scoped` service \(such as `DbContext`\) into its constructor, that) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 360.5 Td (scoped service becomes captured forever as a singleton, causing concurrency collisions and stale) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 349.0 Td (data across multiple HTTP requests. ASP.NET Core solves this by allowing method injection into) Tj ET
