BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 752.0 Td (**Assuming MVC Action Filters Work in Minimal APIs**: Applying an `IActionFilter`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 741.0 Td (attribute to a Minimal API endpoint. Minimal APIs do NOT execute MVC filters; they require) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 730.0 Td (`IEndpointFilter`.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 719.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 717.0 Td (**Missing `[ApiController]` on Controllers**: Forgetting `[ApiController]` on standard) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 706.0 Td (controllers forces manual checks: `if \(!ModelState.IsValid\) return) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 695.0 Td (BadRequest\(ModelState\);`.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 682.0 Td (11. Real-World Production Problem: Silent Security Bypass with Action Filters) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 670.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 668.0 Td (**Incident**: An enterprise team migrated several sensitive financial endpoints from) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 657.0 Td (Controllers to Minimal APIs to improve throughput. A custom `[ApiKeyAuthorizeFilter]` \(an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 646.0 Td (`IAsyncActionFilter`\) had been protecting these endpoints on the old controller.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 635.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 633.0 Td (**Root Cause**: The developer pasted the attribute onto the Minimal API mapping) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 622.0 Td (\(`app.MapPost\("/transfer", ...\).WithMetadata\(new ApiKeyAuthorizeFilter\(\)\)`\). Because) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 611.0 Td (Minimal APIs bypass the MVC `ActionInvoker` pipeline, the `IAsyncActionFilter` was) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 600.0 Td (**silently ignored**, leaving the endpoint completely unauthenticated in production.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 589.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 587.0 Td (**Resolution**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 574.0 Td (Migrated the security logic from `IAsyncActionFilter` to an `IEndpointFilter` and integrated it) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 562.5 Td (using `.AddEndpointFilter<ApiKeyEndpointFilter>\(\)`.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 547.0 Td (12. Interview Preparation Master Questions) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 535.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 533.0 Td (**Basic:** *What is the primary advantage of Minimal APIs over traditional Controllers in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 522.0 Td (ASP.NET Core?*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 509.0 Td (**Answer:** Minimal APIs eliminate the architectural overhead of controllers \(no controller) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 497.5 Td (instantiation, no action invoker pipeline, no heavy reflection\), resulting in significantly) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 486.0 Td (higher request throughput, up to 70% lower memory allocations, faster startup times, and simpler) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 474.5 Td (code structure.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 461.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 459.0 Td (**Intermediate:** *What features does the `[ApiController]` attribute provide out of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 448.0 Td (box in Controllers?*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 435.0 Td (**Answer:** The `[ApiController]` attribute provides: \(1\) Automatic HTTP 400 Bad Request) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 423.5 Td (validation response when `ModelState.IsValid == false`, \(2\) Automatic parameter source inference) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 412.0 Td (\(`[FromBody]` for complex types, `[FromRoute]` for route parameters\), \(3\) Problem Details \(RFC) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 400.5 Td (7807\) standard error responses, and \(4\) Multipart/form-data request inference.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 387.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 385.0 Td (**Senior:** *How do Endpoint Filters in Minimal APIs compare to Action Filters in MVC?*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 372.0 Td (**Answer:** While both provide pre- and post-invocation interception, Endpoint Filters) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 360.5 Td (implement `IEndpointFilter` and operate directly on `EndpointFilterInvocationContext` within the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 349.0 Td (lightweight endpoint pipeline. Action Filters implement `IActionFilter` and are tightly bound to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 337.5 Td (the MVC `ActionExecutingContext` and `ActionInvoker`. Endpoint Filters can be applied to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 326.0 Td (individual endpoints or entire `RouteGroupBuilder` instances, are compatible with Native AOT,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 314.5 Td (and do not incur controller activation overhead.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 301.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 299.0 Td (**Tricky Question:** *Can Minimal APIs support Native AOT \(Ahead-of-Time compilation\) in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 288.0 Td (.NET 8? Why can't traditional Controllers support it easily?*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 275.0 Td (**Best Answer:** Yes, .NET 8 Minimal APIs fully support Native AOT via the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 263.5 Td (`RequestDelegateGenerator` \(RDG\) source generator, which analyzes endpoints at compile-time and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 252.0 Td (generates direct C# code for parameter binding and JSON serialization. Controllers cannot easily) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 240.5 Td (support Native AOT because they fundamentally rely on runtime reflection, dynamic code) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 229.0 Td (generation, and runtime type scanning across assemblies to instantiate controllers, bind models,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 217.5 Td (and invoke actions.) Tj ET
