0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 417.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 415.0 Td (**Senior:** *Why would you implement an `IResourceFilter` instead of an `IActionFilter`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 404.0 Td (for caching?*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 391.0 Td (**Answer:** An `IResourceFilter` executes before the Model Binding stage in the MVC pipeline.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 379.5 Td (If a cached response is found, the resource filter can set `context.Result`, immediately) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 368.0 Td (short-circuiting the pipeline. This bypasses model binding, parameter deserialization, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 356.5 Td (validation completely, saving significant CPU cycles and memory allocations under heavy traffic.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 343.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 341.0 Td (**Tricky Question:** *Can an `IExceptionFilter` catch exceptions thrown inside an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 330.0 Td (`IResultFilter` or inside a custom middleware?*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 317.0 Td (**Best Answer:** **No.** An `IExceptionFilter` only catches exceptions that originate during) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 305.5 Td (the execution of controller actions, action filters, and model binding. If an exception occurs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 294.0 Td (in an `IResultFilter` \(such as JSON serialization errors when streaming to the client\) or in any) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 282.5 Td (upstream middleware, the Exception Filter is completely bypassed. For comprehensive error) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 271.0 Td (capture, always use `UseExceptionHandler\(\)` middleware.) Tj ET
