BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 790.0 Td (**Tricky Question:** *Why can't you inject `IOptionsSnapshot<T>` into a Singleton service) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 779.0 Td (or BackgroundService? What should you use instead?*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 766.0 Td (**Best Answer:** `IOptionsSnapshot<T>` is registered with a **Scoped** lifetime because it is) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 754.5 Td (designed to recompute configuration values per HTTP request. Injecting it into a Singleton) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 743.0 Td (causes a Captive Dependency error \(`InvalidOperationException`\). To monitor dynamic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 731.5 Td (configuration changes inside a Singleton or background worker, you must inject) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 720.0 Td (`IOptionsMonitor<T>`, which is a Singleton and provides live updates via its `CurrentValue`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 708.5 Td (property and `OnChange` event listener.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 693.0 Td (---) Tj ET
