BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 308.0 Td (1. Definition) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 294.0 Td (**Global Exception Handling** in ASP.NET Core is the centralized architectural pattern of) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 282.5 Td (capturing, logging, and translating unhandled runtime errors into standardized, secure HTTP) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 271.0 Td (error responses without leaking internal infrastructure details. In modern .NET 8, this is) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 259.5 Td (implemented using the **`IExceptionHandler`** interface combined with **`UseExceptionHandler`**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 248.0 Td (middleware and the **RFC 7807 Problem Details** specification.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 232.5 Td (2. Historical Reason) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 218.5 Td (In classic ASP.NET and early .NET Core versions:) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 205.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 203.0 Td (Developers wrapped controllers in repetitive `try-catch` blocks or wrote custom MVC) Tj ET
