BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 503.0 Td (**Why Middleware Handling Beats Controller `try-catch`**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 490.0 Td (Writing `try-catch` in every controller action creates massive code duplication, obscures) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 478.5 Td (business logic, and makes changing error contracts across hundreds of endpoints nearly) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 467.0 Td (impossible. Centralized handling guarantees 100% consistent error schemas.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 453.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 451.5 Td (**Why `IExceptionHandler` in .NET 8 Beats Legacy `UseExceptionHandler\(subApp\)`**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 438.5 Td (Prior to .NET 8, configuring error handling required writing nested lambdas in) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 427.0 Td (`app.UseExceptionHandler\(errorApp => errorApp.Run\(...\)\)`. This made dependency injection) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 415.5 Td (cumbersome and unit testing difficult. `IExceptionHandler` classes are first-class injectable) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 404.0 Td (types that can be unit tested in isolation.) Tj ET
