0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 376.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 374.5 Td (**Exception Creation Overhead**: Throwing exceptions in .NET is expensive because the CLR) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 363.5 Td (captures the full stack trace \(`StackWalk`\). Do not use exceptions for routine control) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 352.5 Td (flow \(e.g., standard input validation\); use the **Result Pattern** \(`Result<T>`\) for) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 341.5 Td (expected business failures, and reserve exceptions for truly exceptional errors.) Tj ET
