BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 790.0 Td (8. Design Reasoning) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 778.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 776.0 Td (**Cache-Aside Pattern Mechanics**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 763.0 Td (The application code manages cache reads and writes directly. It queries the cache first; if) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 751.5 Td (missing, it fetches from the source of truth \(database\) and backfills the cache. This ensures) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 740.0 Td (that a temporary cache failure does not crash the application-it gracefully falls back to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 728.5 Td (database.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 715.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 713.0 Td (**Why Output Caching in .NET 8 Beats Legacy Response Caching**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 700.0 Td (Legacy `ResponseCaching` relied entirely on HTTP 1.1 client headers \(`Cache-Control`\) and did) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 688.5 Td (not support server-driven invalidation. .NET 8 Output Caching provides **Cache Tags** for) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 677.0 Td (instant selective purging and **Resource Locking** to automatically prevent stampedes on slow) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 665.5 Td (endpoints.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 650.0 Td (9. Performance Considerations) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 638.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 636.0 Td (**Memory Pressure in `IMemoryCache`**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 623.0 Td (Always set a `SizeLimit` on `MemoryCacheOptions` and specify `SetSize\(1\)` on cache entries.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 611.5 Td (Unbounded `IMemoryCache` is the #1 cause of Out-Of-Memory \(OOM\) crashes in production .NET) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 600.0 Td (applications.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 586.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 584.5 Td (**Serialization Overhead**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 571.5 Td (`IDistributedCache` requires serialization \(`System.Text.Json` or `MessagePack`\). For) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 560.0 Td (ultra-high performance, serialize to binary byte arrays using MessagePack to reduce Redis) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 548.5 Td (network payload size and CPU serialization cycles by ~60%.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 533.0 Td (10. Common Mistakes) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 521.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 519.0 Td (**Cache Stampede \(Thundering Herd\)**: Allowing 5,000 concurrent threads to hit the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 508.0 Td (database when a popular cache key expires simultaneously, causing database connection pool) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 497.0 Td (exhaustion.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 486.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 484.0 Td (**Missing Cache Eviction on Updates**: Updating an entity in the database but forgetting) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 473.0 Td (to invalidate its cache key or output cache tag, causing users to see stale data.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 462.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 460.0 Td (**Caching Nulls Unintentionally vs Cache Penetration**:) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 449.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 447.0 Td (Failing to cache negative lookups allows malicious attackers to query non-existent IDs,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 436.0 Td (bypassing the cache entirely and hammering the database \(Cache Penetration\). Always cache) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 425.0 Td (a null placeholder with a short TTL \(e.g., 30 seconds\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 412.0 Td (11. Real-World Production Problem: The Black Friday OOM Server Crash) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 400.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 398.0 Td (**Incident**: A large retail web app suffered a complete outage during a flash sale.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 387.0 Td (Every 15 minutes, the web pods crashed with `OutOfMemoryException`.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 376.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 374.0 Td (**Root Cause**: The developers used `IMemoryCache` to cache user search results, using) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 363.0 Td (the raw search query as the cache key. When 500,000 users entered arbitrary search) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 352.0 Td (queries, millions of unique strings were stored in RAM. Because no `SizeLimit` or memory) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 341.0 Td (eviction policy was configured on `IMemoryCache`, the process heap expanded until the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 330.0 Td (Linux OS OOM-killer killed the container pods.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 319.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 317.0 Td (**Resolution**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 304.0 Td (Configured `SizeLimit = 20_000` on `MemoryCacheOptions`, set sliding expiration of 2 minutes,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 292.5 Td (and offloaded large query results to an external Redis cluster.) Tj ET
