BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 790.0 Td (**Best Answer:** In Protocol Buffers, the serialized wire format identifies fields solely by) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 778.5 Td (their **unique tag number**, never by field name. To preserve compatibility: \(1\) **Never change) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 767.0 Td (the tag number** of an existing field; \(2\) **Never reuse a tag number** from a deleted field) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 755.5 Td (\(use the `reserved` keyword to reserve removed tags and names\); \(3\) Any new fields added must be) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 744.0 Td (optional \(the default in proto3\), allowing old clients to ignore unknown new fields and new) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 732.5 Td (clients to read old payloads with default values.) Tj ET
