0.85 0.88 0.92 RG 0.5 w 60 642.0 m 545 642.0 l S
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 626.0 Td (1. Definition) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 612.0 Td (**Rate Limiting** in ASP.NET Core is a built-in traffic shaping and defensive mechanism) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 600.5 Td (\(introduced in .NET 7 via `System.Threading.RateLimiting` and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 589.0 Td (`Microsoft.AspNetCore.RateLimiting`\) that controls the rate at which incoming HTTP requests are) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 577.5 Td (processed. It protects applications from Denial of Service \(DoS\) attacks, brute-force password) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 566.0 Td (cracking, API scraping, and cascading resource exhaustion by throttling clients with **HTTP 429) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 554.5 Td (Too Many Requests**.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 539.0 Td (2. Historical Reason) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 525.0 Td (In earlier versions of ASP.NET Core:) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 511.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 509.5 Td (Developers relied on third-party libraries \(such as `AspNetCoreRateLimit`\) or offloaded) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 498.5 Td (rate limiting entirely to API Gateways \(Envoy, Nginx, Azure API Management\).) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 487.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 485.5 Td (Third-party in-app libraries suffered from thread synchronization bottlenecks, memory) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 474.5 Td (leaks, and inconsistent algorithms.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 463.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 461.5 Td (In .NET 7, Microsoft introduced a high-performance, lock-free rate limiting library) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 450.5 Td (directly into the BCL \(`System.Threading.RateLimiting`\), making rate limiting a core,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 439.5 Td (zero-dependency middleware feature.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 426.5 Td (3. Problem It Solves) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 414.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 412.5 Td (**DoS & Resource Exhaustion Defense**: Prevents malicious actors or buggy client loops) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 401.5 Td (from overwhelming database connection pools and CPU threads.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 390.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 388.5 Td (**SaaS Multi-Tenant Tiering**: Enforces commercial subscription limits \(e.g., Free Tier:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 377.5 Td (10 req/min; Enterprise Tier: 5,000 req/min\).) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 366.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 364.5 Td (**Endpoint Concurrency Shielding**: Limits concurrency on computationally heavy endpoints) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 353.5 Td (\(e.g., PDF generation, ML inference\) to avoid thrashing CPU caches.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 340.5 Td (4. Internal Working: The 4 Core Algorithms) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 326.5 Td (ASP.NET Core provides four built-in rate-limiting algorithms:) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 313.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 311.0 Td (**Fixed Window Limiter**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 298.0 Td (Divides time into fixed intervals \(e.g., 1 minute\). Allows a maximum of $N$ requests per) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 286.5 Td (window.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 273.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 271.0 Td (*Flaw*: Vulnerable to **Boundary Bursts** \(e.g., client sends 100 requests at 11:59:59) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 260.0 Td (and another 100 at 12:00:01, totaling 200 requests within 2 seconds\).) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 249.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 247.0 Td (**Sliding Window Limiter**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 234.0 Td (Divides the window into multiple discrete segments \(e.g., a 1-minute window divided into six) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 222.5 Td (10-second segments\). As time moves forward, the window slides, smoothing out bursts and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 211.0 Td (preventing boundary spikes.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 197.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 195.5 Td (**Token Bucket Limiter**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 182.5 Td (A bucket holds a maximum number of tokens. Every request consumes 1 token. Tokens are) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 171.0 Td (replenished continuously at a fixed refill rate.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 157.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 155.5 Td (*Advantage*: Allows controlled **traffic bursts** up to bucket capacity while maintaining) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 144.5 Td (a strict long-term average rate.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 133.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 131.5 Td (**Concurrency Limiter**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 118.5 Td (Limits the number of **simultaneously active in-flight requests** regardless of time. Once the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 107.0 Td (maximum active concurrency is reached, subsequent requests are queued or rejected until active) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 95.5 Td (requests complete.) Tj ET
