0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 284.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 282.5 Td (**Why Scoped and not Transient?** If `DbContext` were Transient, injecting it into) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 271.5 Td (`OrderService` and `PaymentService` within the same HTTP request would produce two) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 260.5 Td (independent contexts with two separate Identity Maps and two separate transaction scopes,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 249.5 Td (breaking the Unit of Work pattern entirely.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 238.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 236.5 Td (**Why not Singleton?** A Singleton `DbContext` would share its Identity Map across all) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 225.5 Td (users globally. User A could see User B's uncommitted cached data. Furthermore, concurrent) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 214.5 Td (HTTP requests would hit the non-thread-safe context simultaneously, crashing the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 203.5 Td (application with `InvalidOperationException`.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 192.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 190.5 Td (**The Captive Dependency Bug:** If a developer injects a Scoped `DbContext` into a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 179.5 Td (Singleton service \(like a Background Worker or RabbitMQ Consumer\), the `DbContext`) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 168.5 Td (instance is "captured" forever, never disposed, accumulates thousands of tracked entities) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 157.5 Td (in its Identity Map \(leaking memory\), and throws concurrency exceptions when multiple) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 146.5 Td (consumer threads execute.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 133.5 Td (9. Performance Impact) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 121.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 119.5 Td (**Standard `AddDbContext`:** 10,000 requests allocate 10,000 `DbContext` instances,) Tj ET
