BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 633.0 Td (*Remedy:* Use `_context.Claims.AddRange\(records\)` \(which calls `DetectChanges` only once at the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 621.5 Td (end\) or set `_context.ChangeTracker.AutoDetectChangesEnabled = false;` during the loop, or use) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 610.0 Td (modern EF Core 7+ bulk techniques.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 594.5 Td (12. Interview Preparation) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 582.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 580.5 Td (**Basic:** *What are the five states of an entity in EF Core?*) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 569.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 567.5 Td (**Answer:** `Detached`, `Unchanged`, `Added`, `Modified`, and `Deleted`.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 556.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 554.5 Td (**Intermediate:** *What does `ChangeTracker.DetectChanges\(\)` do, and when is it called) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 543.5 Td (automatically?*) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 532.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 530.5 Td (**Answer:** It compares the current property values of all tracked entities with their) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 519.5 Td (original values stored in the snapshot buffer. It is automatically triggered by methods) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 508.5 Td (such as `SaveChangesAsync\(\)`, `Entries\(\)`, and `ChangeTracker.HasChanges\(\)`.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 497.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 495.5 Td (**Senior:** *What is the difference between `context.Update\(entity\)` and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 484.5 Td (`context.Attach\(entity\)` for disconnected entities?*) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 473.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 471.5 Td (**Answer:** `context.Update\(entity\)` traverses the entire object graph and sets the state) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 460.5 Td (of every entity and every property to `EntityState.Modified`, causing a massive SQL UPDATE) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 449.5 Td (statement affecting all columns. `context.Attach\(entity\)` puts the entity into the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 438.5 Td (`Unchanged` state; mutations are only tracked if properties are modified subsequent to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 427.5 Td (attachment or explicitly marked via `Entry\(e\).Property\(...\).IsModified = true`.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 416.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 414.5 Td (**Tricky Question:** *If you load an entity, modify a property, and then change it back) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 403.5 Td (to its original value before calling `SaveChanges\(\)`, does EF Core execute a database) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 392.5 Td (query?*) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 381.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 379.5 Td (**Answer:** No. When `DetectChanges\(\)` runs, it compares the current value with the) Tj ET
