0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 458.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 456.0 Td (**Answer:** It occurs when an application executes 1 query to fetch parent records and) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 445.0 Td (then $N$ separate queries to fetch related child data inside a loop. It can be detected) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 434.0 Td (using logging \(`Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Database.Command`\), SQL Profiler, or) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 423.0 Td (OpenTelemetry tracing.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 412.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 410.0 Td (**Intermediate:** *How does `.Include\(\)` resolve the N+1 problem, and what new problem) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 399.0 Td (can it introduce?*) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 388.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 386.0 Td (**Answer:** It performs a SQL `LEFT JOIN` to fetch parent and child records in a single) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 375.0 Td (database roundtrip. However, including multiple child collections introduces **Cartesian) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 364.0 Td (Explosion**, where the relational result set multiplies row counts exponentially, creating) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 353.0 Td (massive memory and network overhead.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 342.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 340.0 Td (**Senior:** *When should you prefer `.AsSplitQuery\(\)` over a single query with) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 329.0 Td (`.Include\(\)`, and what are its concurrency risks?*) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 318.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 316.0 Td (**Answer:** Use `.AsSplitQuery\(\)` when including multiple sibling collections to prevent) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 305.0 Td (Cartesian explosion and reduce network payload size. **Risk:** Because multiple queries) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 294.0 Td (execute non-atomically, if a concurrent transaction modifies the database between query 1) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 283.0 Td (\(Orders\) and query 2 \(OrderItems\), the application could end up with an inconsistent) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 272.0 Td (in-memory state.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 261.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 259.0 Td (**Tricky Question:** *Why is DTO projection with `.Select\(\)` almost always superior to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 248.0 Td (`.Include\(\)` for read-only Web APIs?*) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 237.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 235.0 Td (**Answer:** `.Select\(\)` translates to an exact SQL projection fetching only the specific) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 224.0 Td (columns needed by the API contract \(avoiding `SELECT *`\), automatically joins tables) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 213.0 Td (without Cartesian explosion, completely bypasses Change Tracker overhead, and avoids) Tj ET
