BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 631.0 Td (1. Definition) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 617.0 Td (**EF Core Migrations** is a set of tooling and runtime APIs that allow developers to evolve) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 605.5 Td (their relational database schema incrementally to keep it in sync with the C# data model while) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 594.0 Td (preserving existing application data.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 578.5 Td (2. Historical Reason) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 564.5 Td (Historically, database schema changes were managed through disparate, untracked `.sql` scripts) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 553.0 Td (executed manually by DBAs. This led to "environment drift" where Staging differed from) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 541.5 Td (Production. Early EF introduced database initializers \(`DropCreateDatabaseIfModelChanges`\),) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 530.0 Td (which destroyed production databases if a column was added! EF Core replaced this with a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 518.5 Td (deterministic, source-controlled migration history pipeline.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 503.0 Td (3. Problem It Solves) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 491.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 489.0 Td (**Environment Parity:** Guarantees that local development, QA, Staging, and Production) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 478.0 Td (databases are upgraded through the exact same deterministic sequence of schema mutations.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 467.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 465.0 Td (**Auditability:** Every schema modification \(`Up` and `Down`\) is compiled into C# source) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 454.0 Td (code and committed to Git.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 443.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 441.0 Td (**Zero Data Loss:** Safely migrates schemas with existing enterprise data.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 428.0 Td (4. Internal Working) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 416.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 414.0 Td (**`ModelSnapshot` \(`DbContextModelSnapshot.cs`\):** Whenever a migration is added, EF Core) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 403.0 Td (updates this snapshot file, which reflects the *complete current state* of the EF model.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 392.0 Td (When you run `dotnet ef migrations add`, EF Core does **not** inspect the database; it) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 381.0 Td (compares your current C# `DbContext` code against the `ModelSnapshot` to compute the diff!) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 370.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 368.0 Td (**`__EFMigrationsHistory` Table:** EF Core creates a metadata table in the database with) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 357.0 Td (columns `MigrationId` \(timestamp + name\) and `ProductVersion`. Before executing a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 346.0 Td (migration, it checks whether the `MigrationId` already exists in this table.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 335.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 333.0 Td (**Why `context.Database.Migrate\(\)` at Startup is an Anti-Pattern in Production:**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 320.0 Td (Calling `context.Database.Migrate\(\)` in `Program.cs` when containers boot in Kubernetes creates) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 308.5 Td (catastrophic race conditions. If 10 microservice pods start simultaneously, all 10 attempt to) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 297.0 Td (run `ALTER TABLE` DDL queries against the database at the same time! This results in deadlocks,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 285.5 Td (failed startup health checks, crash-loop backoffs, and potentially corrupted schema metadata.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 272.0 3 3 re f
