BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 790.0 Td (8. Design Reasoning) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 778.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 776.0 Td (**Why are migrations stored as C# code and not raw SQL?** Storing migrations in C# allows) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 765.0 Td (them to be database-agnostic. The exact same C# migration file can emit T-SQL for SQL) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 754.0 Td (Server in production and PostgreSQL or SQLite dialect for local integration testing.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 741.0 Td (9. Performance Considerations) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 729.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 727.0 Td (**DDL Locks:** Adding a column with a non-constant default value or modifying a column) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 716.0 Td (data type in SQL Server requires a schema-modification \(`Sch-M`\) lock, which blocks all) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 705.0 Td (read and write queries on that table for the duration of the DDL execution! For) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 694.0 Td (multi-million-row tables, always add columns as nullable first to avoid long-running) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 683.0 Td (locks.) Tj ET
