BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 246.5 Td (**Senior:** *How do you implement a zero-downtime database migration when a column needs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 235.5 Td (to be renamed?*) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 224.5 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 222.5 Td (**Answer:** By using the **Expand and Contract pattern**: First, add the new column as) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 211.5 Td (nullable alongside the old column. Deploy an application version that dual-writes to both) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 200.5 Td (columns. Run a background script to backfill historical data. Deploy a second application) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 189.5 Td (version that reads and writes exclusively from the new column. Finally, deploy a migration) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 178.5 Td (that drops the old column.) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 167.5 3 3 re f
