BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 108.0 Td (NULL\)`. If no match is found among non-null values, the expression resolves to `NOT \(FALSE) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 97.0 Td (OR UNKNOWN\)`, which evaluates to `NOT \(UNKNOWN\) = UNKNOWN`. Because a `WHERE` clause) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 86.0 Td (requires `TRUE` to return a row, all rows are discarded. The solution is to use `NOT) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 75.0 Td (EXISTS` or filter out `NULL` values in the subquery \(`WHERE Val IS NOT NULL`\).) Tj ET
