BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 314.5 Td (A Saga is a sequence of **local transactions**, each publishing events or messages to trigger) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 303.0 Td (the next step. If any step fails, compensating transactions are executed to undo previously) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 291.5 Td (completed steps.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.35 0.45 0.55 rg 50 276.0 Td (10.2 Why Not Two-Phase Commit \(2PC\)?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 262.0 Td (2PC \(distributed transaction\) requires all participating services to hold locks until the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.8 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 50 250.5 Td (coordinator confirms. In a microservices environment with dozens of services:) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 237.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 235.0 Td (**Lock contention:** Everything grinds to a halt) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 224.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 222.0 Td (**Coordinator becomes SPOF:** If coordinator crashes mid-commit, all participants hang) Tj ET
0.2 0.5 0.85 rg 53 211.0 3 3 re f
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.18 0.2 0.25 rg 62 209.0 Td (**Cross-DB impossible:** 2PC works between same DB vendor \(e.g., SQL Server ? SQL Server\)) Tj ET
